# Datalog in lambda plus merge, with no label: scored points of the
# label-free family.
#
# THE ENCODING. The constants 0 .. N-1 are Scott unary numerals, let bound
# one after another (contest_merge_graph.pl, numeral_lets/4). A binary
# relation is a curried Church Boolean, \x. \y. flag(x, y), a nested case
# on both numerals (numeral_case/3), true exactly on its facts. A rule is
# a curried Boolean function built from:
# - conjunction, and = \p. \q. p q false;
# - existence over the constants, exists = \f. [f c0, ..., f c(N-1)],
#   the merge of the Booleans (a merge read as the predicate's or);
# - disjunction of a rule's bodies, a merge.
# So a join is an existence over the whole universe, the naive join of
# Datalog evaluated top-down, where the labeled family
# (contest_inheritance_datalog.pl) walked tries by label.
#
# THE RULES:
# - transitive closure: path x z = [edge x z, exists (\y. and (edge x y)
#   (path y z))];
# - reachability in the symmetric closure: sym x y = [edge x y, edge y x],
#   reach x z = [sym x z, exists (\y. and (sym x y) (reach y z))].
# Both are recursive by self-application, and the test reads the Church
# Boolean of the rule at the asked tuple. Only Booleans are merged.
#
# THE RELATIONS, chosen so that the existence, which tries the constants in
# order, meets a cycle before the way out:
# - two rings of n constants each: 0 -> 1 -> ... -> n-1 -> 0, n-1 -> n,
#   and n -> ... -> 2n-1 -> n; the tuple is path(0, 2n-1). At n-1 the
#   existence tries 0, back into the first ring, before n;
# - a line 0 -> 1 -> ... -> n-1; the tuple is reach(0, n-1). At every
#   constant the existence tries the one before it first.
# weak_head runs around the first cycle; tabling completes it.
#
# THE REFERENCE is the least fixpoint of the rule by semi-naive Datalog
# evaluation in Prolog (reference_holds/4), the expected algorithm.
#
# The sizes are n, 2n and 4n with a frontier beyond: two rings of 3, 6 and
# 12 constants each, and 24; the line of 4, 8 and 16 constants, and 32.
#
# READINGS (2026-09-28, CPU 2 under contest_limited.sh, a fresh process per
# reading, the boolean(true) template, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB):
# - weak_head runs around the first cycle and is stopped on every point.
# - tabling(weak_head): two rings of 3, 6 and 12 in 29, 236 and 3659 ms,
#   of 24 stopped (7149 ms); the line of 4, 8 and 16 in 13, 66 and 671 ms,
#   of 32 stopped (6791 ms). A doubling costs 8 to 16: every step of the
#   closure tries the whole universe, where semi-naive evaluation joins
#   only the new tuples.
# - records_routed(record_interned(tabling(weak_head)), weak_head): within
#   about 10 per cent of tabling(weak_head), stopped on the same frontier.
# The frontier readings stop before 10 s, as the graph family's did: the
# memory the global store holds outside the limits.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - semi-naive evaluation of the rule's least fixpoint: F. Bancilhon, R.
#   Ramakrishnan, An Amateur's Introduction to Recursive Query Processing
#   Strategies, SIGMOD 1986, doi:10.1145/16856.16859.
# - tabled evaluation: W. Chen, D. S. Warren, Tabled Evaluation with
#   Delaying for General Logic Programs, J. ACM 1996,
#   doi:10.1145/227595.227597.

#   THE POINTS.
#
# The shape is a constructor of merge_datalog/shape, two_rings or line.
# Each other text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "merge_datalog") "shape")
λ two_rings line
. export
λ
